# Land Equilibrium replaces the entry of each land an opponent with at least as many lands puts onto the battlefield: Bot2,
# with one land to Bot1's none (more, not only as many), puts two lands onto the battlefield at once with Reach the Horizon.
# Both enter together, each modified to "puts that land onto the battlefield then sacrifices a land" (CR 614.6), so both
# are there when Bot2 makes the first of its two sacrifices - and it chooses the Plains first, then the Island. Reach the
# Horizon goes on resolving only once both are sacrificed. Bot1's Leyline of the Void exiles every card on its way to Bot2's
# graveyard; Reach the Horizon going there is put by no one, so Land Equilibrium is no replacement Bot2 is asked to order
# with the Leyline's (CR 616.1).
[Bot1 Deck]
Land Equilibrium
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Leyline of the Void
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Reach the Horizon
Forest
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Island
Plains
Swamp x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Land Equilibrium.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Reach the Horizon.Cast
Bot2.Search(Island; Plains)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 3
Bot2.Choose(Plains)
Bot2.Choose(Island)
! Bot2.Replace
[T4 Bot2.End]
[Expect]
Exile = Black Lotus; Island; Plains; Reach the Horizon
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Types = Land
